---
title: "supabase_client_factory (stem-system: Supabase Client Creation)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_route: which client?
    q_route --> q_create_ssr: createClient() - cookie-based SSR
    q_route --> q_create_admin: createAdminClient() - service role

    q_create_ssr --> q_ssr_init: createServerClient(SUPABASE_URL, ANON_KEY, cookies, schema=member)
    q_ssr_init --> q_ssr_config: autoRefreshToken=true, persistSession=true
    q_ssr_config --> [*]: return SSR client (RLS applies via user JWT)

    q_create_admin --> q_check_key: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY defined?
    q_check_key --> q_no_key: missing
    q_check_key --> q_admin_init: present
    q_no_key --> [*]: throw Error
    q_admin_init --> q_js_client: createSupabaseJsClient(SUPABASE_URL, SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, schema=member)
    q_js_client --> q_admin_config: autoRefreshToken=false, persistSession=false
    q_admin_config --> [*]: return admin client (RLS bypassed)

    note right of q_create_admin
        INV-001: admin client uses @supabase/supabase-js directly, NOT @supabase/ssr
        INV-002: SSR client reads user JWT from cookies causing RLS to apply as authenticated role
        INV-003: admin client bypasses RLS entirely via service_role key
    end note

    note right of q_ssr_init
        INV-004: schema is always 'member' and must never be changed
        INV-005: cookie setAll silently catches errors in Server Components
    end note
